MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_001: Whoa, boy! Whoa! You really are a wild one.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_002: All the better. That's how the horse from that Sai\nlegend started out too, until the knight tamed him...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_003: Ah, Gaitz. I thought I heard a commotion, but it's\njust you. Your horse seems rather spry this morning.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_004: Oh, hello, Ursula. I actually just bought him.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_005: Quite the rebel. He's made more than a few riders\ngive up in tears.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_006: Hmm. Is that so...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_007: Were you looking to buy him too?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_008: No, no. However, I think I understand why his\nbehavior seems so unruly.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_009: Hmm?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_010: Aw, poor thing. It appears he's covered in fleas.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_011: He must be so itchy... However, removing them \nshould stabilize his temper.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_012: Really? How did you figure that out?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_013: Well, I simply read his feelings. He's practically\nbegging for your help, Gaitz.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_014: You mean you understood what he was thinking?\nThat's ridiculous.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_015: Perhaps, but he's calling out for you all the same.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_016: And if you intend to be his owner, please take care\nof him. Excuse me.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_017: So, fleas, huh? Is she on to something?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_018: I don't get it, but I suppose it wouldn't hurt to make\nyou an herbal flea remedy.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_019: Gods! Those pests really liked you, huh?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_020: You seem much calmer now. I'm glad the itch\nwent away.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_021: It's too bad you're not actually as wild as they said,\nbut I wouldn't want you to suffer.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_C_022: Looks like Ursula was right all along. Strange.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_001: That ability of yours, understanding animals?\nIt's amazing.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_002: Oh. That's very nice, but I don't think it's as\ncompelling as it seems.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_003: Besides, how precise could it be? It's not as if I can\nactually speak to animals.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_004: Still, it's impressive. I'd like to learn more about\nthis skill.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_005: *sigh* I see... Well, it's not exactly a secret, I suppose.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_006: Great! Well, then, my first question. Did you have to\ndo any training?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_007: Like sitting under a waterfall, or getting buried up to\nthe neck and meditating...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_008: What? Of course it's nothing of the sort! I've simply\nbeen able to do this since I was a child.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_009: For instance... See that stray cat there? I can tell\nshe's hungry.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_010: But she won't go hunting because a child who always\nfeeds her will be by soon.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_011: The child did come! I guess that cat knew it could\nget something better than by scavenging.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_012: You'll have to tell me what other animals\nare thinking.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_013: I want to know the inner thoughts of a war elephant.\nOr, oh! An ornius!
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_014: It's nice you find this interesting, but this is not\na tool for your military exploits.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_015: What did you say?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_016: Come now, you're not who you claim, are you? You\nmay be here as a gladiator, but your true identity is...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_017: You found me out. I guess I underestimated the\nVandahl Trading Company's intelligence network.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_018: Don't worry, I won't pry. And I will keep your\nsecret safe.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_019: But in return, you will stop trying to use me.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_020: I won't. That was never my intention.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_021: I imagine a Brezarant general always keeps an eye\nopen for new methods of controlling the battlefield.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_022: I can respect that. But what I can't respect is\nsomeone who is attempting to use me.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_023: Now you mention it, it would have utility for the\nmilitary. Tending to horses, gathering intelligence...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_024: Now that...I mention it?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_025: Hadn't thought about it. Honestly, I was just\nimpressed. And a little jealous.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_026: I only brought up war elephants because they're what\nI'm familiar with.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_027: I forgot about...well, the "war" part.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_B_028: No, you... Ahem. I see. You're quite carefree for\na military leader...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_001: These stables are spotless.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_002: Our kingdom values its military power. That means\nwe care for our horses and our orniuses.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_003: Quite admirable. There isn't a single soldier among\nyou that doesn't cherish their companions.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_004: Is that what the horses told you?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_005: Yes. Battle is hard on them, but I can sense how\ndedicated they are to press on for you.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_006: It seems you've been able to understand these \nanimals in your own way.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_007: Well, that doesn't stop me from wanting your talent.\nBut yes, my horse and I have a good relationship.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_008: Good. I hope you can hold on to that. War has a way\nof hardening hearts.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_009: And too often, soldiers begin treating their animals\nas servants rather than comrades...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_010: I'll admit, I worried you had fallen into that trap.\nI'm grateful my fears were unfounded here.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_011: I'll keep taking good care of him.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_012: Oh! That voice!
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_013: I thought you might recognize him. This is the horse\nyou told me had fleas.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_014: Not the wild stallion I was hoping for, but he's a\nhard worker alright.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_015: My, you've done quite well as his master, I see.\nCertainly happier than last time we met.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_016: Heh. There, there, you like that, don't you?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_017: Oh, I think I can understand what he's saying.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_018: He remembers you and he appreciates the favor you\ndid for him.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_019: Oh, it wasn't me. Your master did all the hard work.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_020: Ahem! Ursula, your compassion for animals is clearly\nshared in Brezarant.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_021: When the war's over, why not live here?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_022: Live here? Why would I do that?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_023: I heard that you're from a land far from Dagda.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_024: Maybe you should be thinking about a good place to\nput down roots.
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_025: That depends. Are you asking me to move because\nyou think I'd enjoy Brezarant? Or...
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_026: Are you asking for something...more?
MID_SE_Gat_Urs_A_027: Heh. I guess your power doesn't work on humans.